      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Nice to add at least quicky (don’t worry at first about array issue) XMLReader/XMLWriter to data serialize code – so can map xml to/from C++ structs. Note that usual reason to use SAX doesn’t apply here because you can still use sax but if mapping to C++ structs, reading whole thing into memory anyhow. Nice if a way within SAX reader to instantiate XMLReader in a context – so could SAX big flow, and just XMLReader sup-parts?!!! Then combine best of both and maybe not that diff than current SAXObjectReader (which is a problem cuz that’s error prone). Mark in comments more clearlerly SAXOBjectReatder error prone and not recommended!!! (easy to mixup levels - pop error JohnB got yesterday) –LGP 2015-10-06",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
